# Line-ending and text normalisation.
#
# Why this file exists: an SSE framing bug was caused purely by an assumption
# about line endings. The backend emitted CRLF while the frontend parser searched
# for LF LF, so no frame boundary was ever found and every event was buffered into
# one unparsable blob. Mixed endings across a repository make that class of bug easy
# to introduce and hard to see.
#
# Policy: store LF in the repository, check out LF everywhere. The project is
# developed on Windows and Windows tools cope with LF; normalising on commit only
# (leaving CRLF in the working tree) would keep the inconsistency in place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only batch files still need CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.db binary
*.csv binary
*.json.gz binary

# Generated files are excluded from diffs and language statistics: they are
# produced by the build or by indexing, so a diff of them carries no review value.
frontend/dist/** -diff -linguist-generated
reports/knowledge.db -diff -linguist-generated
frontend/package-lock.json -diff -linguist-generated
.cache/** -diff -linguist-generated

# Keep the dataset out of language detection: it is data, not source.
ShuJuYuan/** -linguist-vendored
